Don wrote on Thu, 09 Dec 2004 18:25:23 GMT:

> I think abuses should be tackled head on, rather than tangentially.

Probably the most intelligent thing that has been said in this thread.

> If pudding farming is abusive, then make puddings not split.

The original purpose of the pudding split was to make them challenging 
in an interesting way.  You're fighting a pudding, you hit it twice, 
and ohnoes! now there are three puddings attacking you.  Of course, now 
it is being abused to create infinite puddings and obtain infinite 
death drops, sacrifices, food, intrinsics...

My solution would be to limit each pudding to splitting 3 times.  So a 
single wild pudding could be "farmed" into eight puddings, but no more 
puddings could be created from those 8.

IIRC, currently when a pudding splits each half has 50% of the HP.  I 
suggest that each half should have 70% of the HP.


